## 🔹 Comparison Table (For Freshers)

| Feature | VM | Container | Serverless |
|---------|----|-----------|-----------| 
| **Boot Time** | Minutes | Seconds | Instant |
| **Size** | GB | MB | N/A |
| **Resource Usage** | High | Low | Very Low |
| **Management** | You manage OS | You manage app | AWS manages all |
| **Cost** | Monthly bill | Per usage | Per execution |
| **Best For** | Full apps | Microservices | Event-driven |
| **Example** | EC2 | Docker/ECS | Lambda |

---

## 🔹 When to Use What? (Decision Tree for Freshers)

```
Do you need a full Operating System?
    ├─ YES → Use Virtual Machines (EC2)
    │         (Full control, traditional apps)
    │
    └─ NO → Do you want to manage servers?
              ├─ YES → Use Containers (Docker/ECS)
              │         (Microservices, modern apps)
              │
              └─ NO → Use Serverless (Lambda)
                       (Simple functions, event-driven)
```

